  "lore": "The Mage is a creature of high places and deep silences. You will find them nesting in calcified towers or wherever the veil of reality has worn dangerously thin. Unlike the common predator, the Mage does not hunger for flesh, but for the fundamental truths that bind existence. \n\nThey are ambush hunters of the mind. They weave webs of shifting geometry and whispered paradoxes to ensnare the unwary. Once caught, a victim\u2019s very history may be unraveled, fed upon to fuel the creature\u2019s inner radiance. They do not merely kill; they erase.\n\nIn local folklore, they are feared as the \"Hollow Scholars.\" Mothers warn children that to look a Mage in the eye is to lose one\u2019s reflection to the void. They are seen as harbingers of cosmic indifference, entities that have traded their humanity for the cold light of the stars. To encounter one is to stand before a storm that thinks. Avoid their haunts, traveler, for they do not see men as kin, but as mere ink for their endless, invisible scrolls.",
